statement:
Let $k \ge 1$ and let $\omega_k = e^{2\pi i/k}$ be the primitive $k$-th root of unity. For each $a \in \mathbb{Z}/k\mathbb{Z}$, write $\omega_k^{a}$ for $\omega_k$ raised to the canonical representative of $a$ in $\{0,\ldots,k-1\}$. Then for every $j \in \mathbb{Z}/k\mathbb{Z}$,
\[
  \sum_{a \in \mathbb{Z}/k\mathbb{Z}} \omega_k^{\,j a}
  = \begin{cases} k & \text{if } j = 0, \\ 0 & \text{if } j \neq 0. \end{cases}
\]

replaced:
For $j : \mathbb{Z}/k\mathbb{Z}$,
\[
  \sum_{a \in \mathbb{Z}/k\mathbb{Z}} \omega_k^{j \cdot a}
  = \begin{cases} k & \text{if } j = 0, \\ 0 & \text{if } j \neq 0. \end{cases}
\]
This is the fundamental character-orthogonality identity for $\mathbb{Z}/k\mathbb{Z}$.
